Super-resolution models bundled with PyLithics

These files are the trained ESPCN and FSRCNN models that OpenCV's
dnn_superres module reads. PyLithics uses them to upscale a working copy
of a drawing whose strokes are too thin for detection. The saved crops,
the DPI tags and every measurement stay at the source resolution.

ESPCN_x2.pb, ESPCN_x3.pb, ESPCN_x4.pb
    Source: https://github.com/fannymonori/TF-ESPCN (export/)
    Licence of the repository: Apache License 2.0
    Paper: Shi et al. 2016, "Real-Time Single Image and Video
    Super-Resolution Using an Efficient Sub-Pixel Convolutional Neural
    Network", CVPR.

FSRCNN_x2.pb, FSRCNN_x3.pb, FSRCNN_x4.pb
    Source: https://github.com/Saafke/FSRCNN_Tensorflow (models/)
    Licence of the repository: Apache License 2.0
    Paper: Dong, Loy and Tang 2016, "Accelerating the Super-Resolution
    Convolutional Neural Network", ECCV.

Both repositories are the ones the opencv_contrib dnn_superres README
names as the origin of these models. The files are unchanged. The
FSRCNN files were fetched on 2026-09-29 from the raw URLs of the
Saafke repository (38–42 KB each; a file of about 290 KB in that
place is a saved GitHub web page, not a model).
